The class and related types are internal and inaccessible for direct subclassing or mocking in the test project. Also, the refactor tool is not available to add test seams. Given this, I will write a test that exercises the public SendCheckpointAsync method and verifies the logger calls by mocking ILogger and dependencies as much as possible, without subclassing or accessing internal types directly. I will simulate the scenario by mocking dependencies to cause the code path that logs the error on line 301.

I will submit a test file that mocks the dependencies and verifies the logger.LogError call with the expected message. This will be a black-box test of SendCheckpointAsync that triggers the error logging.

